    category: "Android",
    title: "Zscaler Client Connector 在 Android 與 ChromeOS 上存在本地可利用的緩衝區溢出漏洞 CVE-2026-59566",
    summary: "本篇報告揭露 Zscaler Client Connector 於其在 Android 和 ChromeOS 平台上的版本中，存在一個名為 CVE-2026-59566 的本地可利用緩衝區溢出（buffer overflow）漏洞。該漏洞的攻擊向量為本地 (AV:L)，且無需權限 (PR:N) 或使用者互動 (UI:N)。若被惡意利用，可能導致受影響設備發生本地拒絕服務攻擊 (denial-of-service attack)。根據 CVSS v3.1 的評估，該漏洞的機密性、完整性和可用性都為高風險（C:H/I:H/A:H）。建議使用者應密切關注 Zscaler 官方發布的安全公告，並儘快更新至修補了此漏洞的新版本，以避免遭受攻擊。",
    tags: ["Zscaler Client Connector", "CVE-2026-59566", "Android", "ChromeOS", "緩衝區溢出", "本地漏洞"],
    title_en: "Zscaler Client Connector has locally exploitable buffer overflow vulnerability on Android and ChromeOS (CVE-2026-59566)",
    summary_en: "This report reveals a locally exploitable buffer overflow vulnerability, designated CVE-2026-59566, found in versions of Zscaler Client Connector running on the Android and ChromeOS platforms. The vulnerability has a local attack vector (AV:L), requires no privileges (PR:N), and no user interaction (UI:N). If exploited maliciously, it could lead to a denial-of-service attack on affected devices. According to CVSS v3.1 assessment, the vulnerability poses high risk across confidentiality, integrity, and availability (C:H/I:H/A:H). Users are advised to closely monitor official Zscaler security announcements and update to a patched version promptly to prevent potential attacks.",
